      "content": "It is completely normal to feel overwhelmed when isolation and self-imposed isolation feel contradictory; the silence you are experiencing might actually be a signal that your approach to \"peace\" needs an adjustment. You are safe to explore taking small, gentle steps toward connection that feel comfortable for you, whether that is talking to a trusted friend or asking for a single day of support.\nRemember that getting help from a mental health professional can provide a safe space to untangle these feelings without the fear of \"crushing\" the life you are trying to live.\nYou do not have to build yourself out of the silence alone.\nI hope you find the courage to take one small step today.\nYou are worth the help you deserve.",
